**Two parity gotchas caught and handled**
1. `detect_legacy_configs` returns bare relative paths (`.wai`), so `Path::parent()` is `Some("")` — the old code silently relied on `git -C ""` being a documented no-op. Normalized to `"."` for the root walk.
2. `tracked` relativizes `path == root` to an empty pathspec, which git rejects with exit 128 (old code returned true there); the degenerate case now probes `"."`.

My first dir-path test expectation was wrong (repo-root-as-path walks from *outside* the repo — false in both old and new code); corrected to the real gh#30 subdirectory shape.

